WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:13.100
Another of the most important things that makes search effective is the suggestions and results that can appear while the user searches, as soon as they tap the search bar.

2
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:24.600
Before I even start, suggestions may appear in the search bar itself, as a menu or list under it, and as I type, suggestions can appear based on what I'm typing.

3
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:37.190
This is very important in making search easier: the search suggestions themselves. So we'll go through some notes that can improve them as they appear to the user.

4
00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:46.340
First, as we said, as soon as the user types the query, a dropdown with these suggestions starts to appear so they can pick from it.

5
00:00:46.340 --> 00:01:09.740
These suggestions have many benefits for the user, the first being that they help them reach good results.

6
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:28.140
If they finish the search themselves they may find no results, or results that aren't what they wanted. But if they type a few characters and a suggestion appears, that suggestion most likely has good results in my website or product, so if they pick it and it fits what they're after, they'll get good results.

7
00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:49.340
It matters for interaction cost too: they don't spend mental or physical effort typing everything. As soon as they type a few characters suggestions appear, and if one fits, the interaction cost is very low: a few characters, then straight to choosing.

8
00:01:49.340 --> 00:02:07.740
Also typos: I've spared the user spelling mistakes that could have shown no results, or the wrong ones, because they picked from the suggestions. These are the benefits of using suggestions.

9
00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:22.240
To make suggestions as good as they can be, here are a few tips for search that will help.

10
00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:46.340
First: don't show a suggestion if picking it gives few results, or none related to it in the website or product. If I'm a UI/UX designer at a product company and notice this problem, I should flag it to be fixed.

11
00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:53.540
Because the experience suffers badly if the user picks a suggestion and gets few results; their trust drops and they probably won't try again.

12
00:02:53.540 --> 00:03:09.740
Second important thing about suggestions: I should distinguish the style of the suggestion text, between what the user typed themselves and the completion the website suggested.

13
00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:23.840
For example, if I type "basketball" and the suggestions are "basketball hoop" and others, as a designer I need to distinguish between the word the user typed and the completion the website suggests.

14
00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:45.240
So how do I distinguish them? Do I highlight the suggested part, or what the user typed? Those are two options. Think about it for a minute and let's see the answer together.

15
00:03:45.654 --> 00:03:55.554
Do I highlight what the user typed, or the completion the website suggests?

16
00:03:55.554 --> 00:04:16.654
Now we have two different cases. In one kind of search, when the user types a word, the suggestions only continue that word: if I type "basketball", every suggestion continues it, like "basketball hoop".

17
00:04:16.654 --> 00:04:35.954
In the other kind of search, if I type any word, the suggestions contain it anywhere: at the start, middle or end. So in which case do we highlight the user's text, and in which the suggested text?

18
00:04:36.185 --> 00:05:00.899
In the first case, the suggestions all continue what the user typed, those exact letters, not in the middle or at the end. Like our example: we typed "uxd" and suggestions appeared, all starting with "uxd" and completing it.

19
00:05:00.899 --> 00:05:32.799
Here we highlight the part the website suggests, not the user's part, because the user's part sits in the same place at the start of every option, so they don't need help spotting it. They need to spot the completion, and if it's highlighted they'll see it faster and choose faster.

20
00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:59.899
In the second case, what I typed may be at the start, middle or end, so it isn't lined up. I need the user to see where their text is so they can read what comes before and after it. Suggestions can be long, so I highlight the text the user typed in the search query.

21
00:05:59.899 --> 00:06:11.649
So now we know some tips and guidelines for building suggestions into the search flow, and suggestions are one of the things that make search effective.
